A||||3||Songman||Alabama Swap Meet||||6||
Z||000000||Songman||04-28-2001||10:45 PM||||I just got back to Nashville after a great Fiero Day! It started out with a little Fiero convoy along a very winding road. I'm not even gonna mention some of the speeds that we hit in places where we could. In fact, I couldn't if I want to. I need a higher valued speedometer!<P>As we approached the Fiero Factory, we could see all types of Fieros parked everywhere... an Aldino kit, a Countach kit, stock Fieros and modified. It was fantastic!<P>But of course, the coolest thing was actually meeting the people that I have talked to so often on this forum. From our TN group, we had myself, Keith (ironhedno3), Allan (spideyfoot) and Julia, Fred, Kendall and Frankie, Carroll and Christine... Met some of the GA guys (Wolfhound and Raydar), and the database guy (John)! <P>There were some that I saw and recognized their name but never actually got to meet. <P>Doug brought my Indy down on the way so my day was started off right even with none of the other great stuff of the day! But I fought the urge and went ahead and took the t-top as I had planned. It was a beautiful day for all of this...<P>Of course, I could go on and on, but suffice it to say that it was a great day and I hope many more Fiero events will be planned so we can all keep getting together.<P>I know a lot of people stayed to go back tomorrow, but I have to leave town so I couldn't. I hope other people will share some of their adventures...<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||6
Z||000001||Cooter||04-28-2001||11:36 PM|||| <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Dcp01553.jpg"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Dcp01554.jpg"> <P>I only wish that I had brought more money!||||reg||1
Z||000002||Songman||04-29-2001||12:41 AM||||No doubt! There were a lot of nice cars for sale! Like any car show there are always a lot for sale because people are ready to start on something new!<P>From that Aldino, to that mint Indy on the trailer, to Raydar's Formula.. I would have loved to have had any of them! Instead I just got a few parts and came on home... Oh yeah! I did get a pretty nice sunburn too!<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Raydar||04-30-2001||12:27 PM||||What a great time! <BR>Finally got to put faces with many of the names I've seen here. (And have read several posts from folks that I missed, completely!)  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> <BR>Only spent about half of the funds I brought with me. Bought a few books and bits 'n' pieces. Found a pair of HO scale Fiero slotcars. Even have a trade in the works for the Formula. (Gonna mix up the 2.5 "red" Fiero family with the 3 "black" Fiero Family.)  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>88 T-top Formula<BR>88 soon-to-be-V6 coupe||||reg||14
